Revision history for GobanFTP

1.000  2026-05-19
  - Release v1.0 / package 1.000 as the P14 proof-machine source for
    listing-first Go over enumerable stores, with `GOFTP/1` still anchored on
    descriptor basenames and direct `events/` child basenames.
  - Freeze filename-derived event ids, accepted-basename `event_set_root`,
    DAG construction, conservative replay, `chinese-area-v1` rules, SGF, and
    diagnostics as the shared proof boundary.
  - Ship v1 profiles and runtime read paths for local, FTP, read-only Git tree,
    read-only DNS record-file admission, and WebDAV, while keeping Git publish,
    live DNS, AXFR, DNSSEC trust, provider APIs, and DNS publishing outside the
    release claim.
  - Declare and cover the `ftp-goftp1` tmp+rename publish path with mock FTP
    tests and optional disposable live smoke, while keeping live FTP auth, live
    FTP integrity, and production FTP deployment safety outside the release
    claim.
  - Add cross-substrate witness and golden-vector coverage for root equality,
    replay equality, rule failures, DAG edge cases, ACK recovery, terminal play,
    and public non-consensus poison vectors.
  - Add signed-HMAC witness acceptance, verifier-local `v1 keygen` / `v1 attest`
    operation, explicit trusted-key input, and read-only signed-HMAC overlays
    across the admitted read profiles without changing unsigned `GOFTP/1`.
  - Add fixture publish-purpose token semantics and default-off verifier-local
    publish preflight for local, FTP, and WebDAV publish flows, without claiming
    production key lifecycle, production auth, or real writer authorization.
  - Add local `gobanftp play --tui` terminal play and read-only text, static
    HTML, and static terminal witness surfaces as non-consensus display/input
    layers over existing replay and publish callbacks.
  - Keep source art, optional `Inline::C`, Web-style output, terminal surfaces,
    sidecars, projections, temporary entries, metadata, resource bodies, and
    file bytes outside replay truth.
  - Add final release documentation, manifest hygiene, and `t/p14-claim-audit.t`
    gates so the source tree states the implemented v1.0 boundary while still
    rejecting over-claims for hosted Web UI, Git publish, live DNS, production
    auth, complete JSON output, and complete future attack coverage.
  - Switch repository licensing from the previous `perl_5` distribution terms
    to Apache-2.0 for the code, protocol documentation, examples, fixtures,
    vectors, projections, and static specimens.

0.001  2026-05-17
  - Treat this distribution as the v0.1 hardening/showcase release: the Perl
    package version is `0.001`, while the project milestone name is `v0.1`.
  - Built the initial GOFTP/1 runtime prototype: descriptor and event filename
    parsing, event id calculation, DAG replay, rules validation, SGF output,
    rebuildable projections, local CLI play/publish/watch commands, local
    storage, and a mock-tested FTP store backend.
  - Kept core replay listing-first: descriptor and events/ basenames remain
    authoritative, while file bytes, FTP metadata, sidecars, projections, and
    temporary entries stay outside consensus input.
  - Added ack-assisted fork recovery commands while preserving conservative
    fork diagnostics by default.
  - Added release hygiene rules for Inline::C caches, blib, MYMETA,
    pm_to_blib, generated distributions, and temporary publish/build scratch
    files.
  - Added a minimal replayable example fixture with rebuildable projections.
  - Removed unused JSON::MaybeXS and Path::Tiny runtime dependency
    declarations and synchronized the dependency documentation.
  - Documented make disttest and the requirement to run live FTP tests against
    an isolated, disposable FTP root.
  - Added an opt-in `script/live-ftp-smoke` helper that runs the live FTP tests
    against a temporary localhost pyftpdlib server without making pyftpdlib a
    default test dependency.
  - Documented the v0.1 hardening/showcase boundary: `GOFTP/1` consensus stays
    frozen for the release, and the listing transcript is a replay-derived
    projection rather than a consensus input.
  - Added a browsable `ftp-race-shrine` example fixture that shows a conservative
    fork after an FTP-style race while keeping ack-assisted recovery explicit.
